fact WorkItem(id: "WI-069", description: some(value: "Implement the `Suspension` effect: first-class continuations on the activation stack. WI-050 stubs `Suspension` as UnhandledEffect. Real implementation: (1) `SuspensionHandle` wraps a saved snapshot of the activation stack + locals + in-flight `AwaitState`s. (2) `operation suspend(k: Function[T, U]) -> U effects Suspension` — when invoked, snapshot the current stack up to the suspend site, return the `SuspensionHandle` to user code, bail out of `run()`. (3) `operation resume(handle: SuspensionHandle, value: T) -> U` — restore the saved stack, deliver the value to the saved continuation, resume `run()`. Uses the heap-allocated activation stack from WI-060 (CPS eval) directly — no VM/bytecode needed. The `ClosureHandle` Rc refcount (WI-055) already makes snapshot+restore safe. Scope: save/restore protocol, suspend/resume builtins, test of continuation capture and round-trip.\n\nSeparate from `Branch` (WI-070 — the dangling \"WI-TODO\" this description used to carry): Branch is value-level non-determinism, a different shape. But the two SHARE this ticket's substrate, and 027.2 names this one explicitly.\n\nWHAT ALREADY LANDED, so this is smaller than filed: `Clone` on `Frame` / `ActivationStack` — the multi-shot half of the protocol — is DELIVERED (WI-078 Phase A/a, `eval/frame.rs:164`), and its doc says the clone semantics are exactly what a snapshot needs (shares immutable `Rc<NodeOccurrence>` sub-trees, deep-copies the mutable `locals` / `buffered` vectors, so a snapshot does not alias the live frame's evolving bindings). `NodeOccurrence` is likewise already shaped for continuation capture (`kb/node_occurrence.rs:1076`).\n\nWHAT IS STILL MISSING, and it is the same piece 027.2 needs: a `StepOutcome::Suspend` variant. Today `StepOutcome` is `Done | Continue | Deliver` (`eval/eval.rs:27`). The nearest existing shape is `Done`, the variant that EXITS the trampoline; `Suspend` differs from it only in leaving the activation stack INTACT instead of empty.\n\nWARNING, from WI-455's OWN feedback: proposals 027.2 and 047 cite WI-455 as the precedent for `StepOutcome::Suspend`. THAT PRECEDENT DOES NOT EXIST — WI-455 built `StepOutcome::Dispatch`, proved it green, then DROPPED it, because an OpRef application now resolves in ONE HOP by construction and there was no chain left to hand back to `run()`. Introduce `Suspend` on its own merits.\n\nCONSUMER: WI-070 (`Branch`) needs exactly the Branch slice of this — suspend at a goal, drive SLD, multi-shot resume once per solution (027.2 §\"The eval↔SLD switch\"). Landing the general capability here first is the cheaper order, but WI-070 may also cut its own narrow slice; decide when one of them is claimed.\n\nACCEPTANCE (retained): a continuation is captured and round-trips — DRIVE it (suspend inside a running operation, resume it, assert the delivered value), not \"it loads clean\"; a multi-shot resume of one handle runs the continuation twice with independent state; each test says which case fails when the change is backed out. `cargo-test` green via `rustland/scripts/test.sh`."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-050", "WI-060"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Open)
